GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC13): the polygons just past the picture's edges kept for the cast
shadows.

- The sun is in the north, so every shadow falls down the screen (or aside, morning and evening):
  a tall building or a row of trees just above the picture shadows the ground in view. Walking up,
  those shadows popped in as their casters came in (the user, at noon toward Sprout Tower).
- The steady overworld's guard band drops a polygon wholly past one of the picture's edges (never
  drawn; kept, they overflowed polygon RAM in the Ruins of Alph). Those above the picture (to a
  screen up) and beside it (to half a screen) are now kept (GPU3D::OffscreenPoly: clip and texture
  coordinates, screen positions by the guard band's arithmetic past the edges, attributes; at
  most 4096 a scene) beside polygon RAM, swapped with the scene; the picture in between has its
  replay's. None below: nothing there shadows the picture (a light's shadows point away from it
  too). The shadow geometry (patch 0028) gives them as polygons flagged ShadowOffscreen: casters
  only.
- The game draws a map prop (a building, Sprout Tower) only when its box passes the hardware box
  test (map_prop_manager.c), so a tall building just above the screen sent nothing. In the steady
  overworld a box now passes up to half a screen above the picture and a quarter screen either
  side (BoxTest); only drawing follows a box test there, and what's past the edges is dropped and
  kept as above. Further (a screen up, half aside) the game drew late now and then (a frame shown
  twice walking up Violet City).

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).
